# Build products (regenerated by make). `/build/*` is a blanket exclude
# and every SOURCE file under build/ has to earn its way back in below -
# easy to forget when adding one.
#
# build/watcom/{cli,clidos,dll,gui} are OBJECT DIRECTORIES (verified with
# `file`: they are directories of .obj, not scripts - the Watcom recipes
# live in the Makefile). gen_exports.py is the one real source file in
# there, a DLL build-time dependency.
#
# build/arm/*.sh, build/mips/*.sh, build/x87/*.sh, build/ci.sh and
# build/dedupe_gate.sh are SOURCE: the ARM cross-build, the QEMU runner,
# the x86-vs-ARM bit-identity gate, the MIPS big-endian/little-endian
# cross-build and its bit-identity gate, the 32-bit x87 gcc build
# (AOSC OS / Afterglow), the CI entry point and the shared-helper dedupe
# gate (task #31).
# A blanket exclude that swallows them means `git clean` deletes the
# gates and a fresh clone never sees them, and gates that do not survive
# a clone are not gates. Re-include the DIRECTORY before its contents:
# git does not descend into an excluded directory, so `!/build/arm/*.sh`
# alone does not work. dedupe_gate.sh learned this the hard way: it sat
# in a `git add -A` and a commit with no error, invisible until the
# next clone (task #31's own commit message wrongly reported it landed -
# see the follow-up commit that actually adds it).

/build/*
!/build/watcom/
/build/watcom/*
!/build/watcom/gen_exports.py
!/build/arm/
!/build/mips/
!/build/x87/
!/build/ci.sh
!/build/dedupe_gate.sh
!/build/dup_body_gate.sh
!/build/c89_floor_gate.sh
!/build/twin_pair_gate.sh
!/build/comment_hygiene_gate.sh
!/build/int_pipeline_arm_gate.sh
!/build/mm_alias_gate.sh
!/build/isa_floor_watcom_gate.sh
!/build/switch_matrix_gate.sh
!/build/switch_matrix_probe.c
!/build/dead_ifndef_gate.sh
!/build/kernel_matrix_gate.sh
!/build/bare_endif_gate.sh
!/build/fixed_tier_xcompiler_gate.sh
!/build/norm_int_gate_tokens_zh.txt
!/build/norm_int_gate_tokens_en.txt
!/build/native_obj_gate.sh
!/build/f32count_billing_gate.sh
!/build/recur_write_float_arm_gate.sh
!/build/subn_gate.sh
!/build/gcc_flag_parity_gate.sh
!/build/changelog_comment_gate.sh
!/build/str_table_order_gate.sh
!/build/align_gate.sh
!/build/codesize_gate.sh
!/build/float_knob_gate.sh
!/build/xcheck_gate.sh
# Comparators, not gates: a gate that ships without the program it
# compares with is a gate that SKIPs in a fresh clone. logit_rms.c and
# the gate scripts above predate this list and are tracked already, so
# the rule never bit them; a NEW one has to be named here.
!/build/nll_paired.c
!/build/gcc_watcom_pair_gate.sh
!/build/dev_timing.sh
!/build/xcc_codesize.sh
!/build/xcc_mnemonics.sh
!/build/div_census.sh
!/build/move_census.sh
!/build/vc4_limits_gate.sh
!/build/gate_wiring_gate.sh
!/build/utf8_escape.py
!/build/vc4_compile_gate.sh
!/build/kv_slot_next_probe.c
!/build/caption_symmetry_gate.sh
!/build/capmetrics.c
!/build/capshot.c
!/build/ppbrace_gate.sh
!/build/ppbrace_census.awk
!/build/o3_probe.sh
!/build/branch_census.sh
!/build/q8pack_mmx_probe.c
!/build/normss_pack_mmx_probe.c
!/build/lerp_q15_probe.c
!/build/exp_q20_probe.c
!/build/dot128_t2_probe.c
!/build/seed_gate.sh
!/build/pair_census.sh
!/build/gcc_warning_gate.sh
!/build/gui_selftest_gate.sh
!/build/t2_probe_stubs.c
!/build/dot128_x16_probe.c
!/build/dot128_q16_probe.c
!/build/ascii_source_gate.sh
!/build/div_hotness.sh
!/build/cov_run.sh

# Stray compiler/linker intermediates (gcc, Open Watcom), plus the raw
# dumps probes drop at the repo root when run without a -o path.
*.o
*.obj
*.err
*.out
*.map
*.lib
*.lst
*.mbr
*.sym
# gcov's notes, data and annotated listings. build/branch_census.sh has
# to run gcov from the repo root - it resolves source paths relative to
# the current directory - so the .gcov land here and are swept into a
# temp dir. These catch whatever a killed run leaves behind.
*.gcov
*.gcda
*.gcno

# Binaries
/llama98
/llama98.exe
/llama98-w.exe
/llama98-dos.exe
/llama98.dll
/kunkun98-gui
/kunkun98-gui.exe
/kunkun98-w.exe
/kunkun98-serve
/kunkun98-serve.exe

# wrc/windres resource artifacts
gui/kunkun98.res

# Runtime config written beside the binary (kunkun98.ini, kunkun98-gui.ini,
# kunkun98-w.ini) - machine-local, and carries the classic_ui test switch
kunkun98*.ini

# Claude Code / AI assistant local config (machine-specific, not source).
#
# CLAUDE.md is NOT in this list, and its name is why it nearly was:
# this repository's copy is project documentation - the working rules,
# the build and verify sections, the layering rule. The one document
# whose job is to stop someone working in the wrong tree is the last one
# that should be missing from a fresh clone. The training tree tracks
# its own copy for the same reason.
#
# CLAUDE.local.md stays excluded: that name is the per-machine one.
.claude/
.claude.json
.claude.json.backup
.mcp.json
CLAUDE.local.md
.aider*
.cursor/
.codeium/
.github/copilot-instructions.local.md

# Scratch / working directories
/tmp/
/.tmp/
/.cache/
/scratch/
/worktrees/
/.worktrees/
/out/
/dist/

# Model weights and test fixtures (never committed - too large)
/models/
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.pth

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.orig
*.rej

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Workflow scratch (design notes, plans). This project keeps its
# reasoning at the declaration it belongs to, not in a parallel tree.
docs/superpowers/

# Numeric probes (.prof/), moved here from the deprecated training-side
# tree by user decision; the directory's own README classifies them.
# EXCLUDED DELIBERATELY, with the consequence understood: they are not
# in the remote and a fresh clone does not see them. The same pattern
# applied to tools/kernelgen's generators would be a defect - those are
# source. This one is a decision.
.prof/
